    "q-111791": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111791",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(T)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have that\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111791-a",
